  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that (+)-1,5-Epoxy-nor-ketoguaia-11-ene may interact with prostate cells through multiple pathways. The first pathway links the compound to Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like, which is targeted by WS-5995 B, a known inhibitor of prostate cell proliferation. The second pathway connects the compound to 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14, which is targeted by a complex compound that also affects prostate cells. Both pathways indicate that the compound may exert its effects on prostate cells through mechanisms involving protein modification and degradation. The evidence is consistent with the compound acting as a modulator of cellular processes critical to prostate function, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be fully elucidated. The strength of the evidence is moderate, with the scores reflecting the confidence in the relationships established across the pathways.",
